| §7 standard | agree, with three edits | (a) Sign-in notice → CTA **16**, not 8. (b) Sheet subtitle **8 under the title**. (c) The bar caption line is 8 (Codex has it as "status"). |
| §8 OTP legal links `#` → D-101 config URLs | agree (reference only) | The build already reads them from config (signin-d101). There is nothing to change in the design. |
| §9 questions | partly | "Approve §5 wording" is too broad. I'd ask about **only** the changed lines, in one list. "Use the §7 standard" is not a yes/no Apurva can judge without the after pictures, so it goes with them. |

## Still disputed (after my side)
1. Sign-in notice → Send OTP: **16** (Claude) vs **8** (Codex).
2. Sheet subtitle: **8 under the title** (Claude) vs **16 box gap, ≈ 26 to the title text** (Codex).
3. Offer point 1 wording: "Sign in with one touch / No SMS to wait for." (Claude) vs "No waiting for an OTP" (Codex).
4. Add time always visible: **open** (Claude, Q3) vs **v3 wins** (Codex).
/* Screens audit — the agreed below-band changes, applied on top of the approved pages (after the band audit's after.css)
   for the after-<screen>.png pictures only. Injected at capture time (tools/capture.py after); no approved file changes.
   Tokens only. */

/* OTP: a box notice under the code sits 16 below it, like every result notice under a field (D-98). */
.grp > .note{margin-top:0}
/* OTP: the consent line sits directly above Verify (D-44): 16, like Sign-in's helper -> Send OTP. */
.consent{margin-bottom:0}
/* A result notice directly above the button it came from sits 8 above it (RULES §8.3, A-14: notice <-> button 8). */
/* OTP: with no consent line (locked, expired-and-limited), the notice -> Verify is 8. */
.grp:has(> .note.show) + .grp:not(:has(> .consent.show, > .consent.reserve)){margin-top:var(--tm-space-sm)}
/* Sign-in: a server notice under the field -> Send OTP is 8 (the field -> notice stays 16, D-98). */
#doctor-login-preview .tm-field:has(.login-notice:not([hidden])) + .login-submit{margin-top:var(--tm-space-sm)}

/* Offer: point titles 16/24 semibold (L2 strong), like every other 16/24 emphasis; medium is not on the scale. */
.points .pt-t{font-weight:var(--tm-font-weight-semibold)}

/* Sheets: the subtitle sits 8 under the title, as in the screen band (header row is 48, the 20/28 title is centred in it). */
/* after.js moves the subtitle into the header next to the title; the title keeps its place beside the 48 close button. */
.tm-sheet__header:has(> .tm-sheet__titles){align-items:flex-start}
.tm-sheet__titles{flex:1;min-width:0;padding-top:calc((var(--tm-target-min) - var(--tm-font-lineheight-lg)) / 2)}
.tm-sheet__titles > .tm-sheet__subtitle{margin-top:var(--tm-space-sm)}

/* Add-time sheet: the same picker as Home v3 setup — "Quick picks" over the chips, 32 to "Custom". */
.tm-sheet .picker .qp{margin:0 0 var(--tm-space-sm)}
.tm-sheet .picker .adjust-row{margin-top:var(--tm-space-2xl)}
/* Add-time sheet: the result notice moves into the pinned actions, 16 above Add (A-12, like the bar, A-19). */
.tm-sheet__actions > .sheet-feedback{margin:0 0 var(--tm-space-sm)}

/* Home v3 setup: "Minimum 15 minutes" back on the Custom row (D-40), right-aligned helper. */
.frame .group .lbl.with-help{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline}
.frame .group .lbl .help{font-size:var(--tm-font-size-body-md);line-height:var(--tm-font-lineheight-sm);font-weight:var(--tm-font-weight-regular);color:var(--tm-content-secondary)}
(screen) => {
  // Screens audit — agreed DOM moves for the after pictures only (tools/capture.py after). Copy comes from after-copy.json.
  if (screen === 'home') {
    const sheet = document.querySelector('.tm-sheet');
    // Sheet subtitle sits 8 under its title, inside the header (title + subtitle are one block, as in the band).
    const head = sheet && sheet.querySelector('.tm-sheet__header'), sub = sheet && sheet.querySelector('.tm-sheet__body > .tm-sheet__subtitle:first-child');
    if (head && sub && !head.querySelector('.tm-sheet__titles')) {
      const box = document.createElement('div'); box.className = 'tm-sheet__titles';
      box.append(head.querySelector('.tm-sheet__title'), sub); head.prepend(box);
    }
    const picker = sheet && sheet.querySelector('.picker');
    if (picker && !picker.querySelector('.qp')) {   // the same picker as Home v3 setup: "Quick picks" over the chips
      const qp = document.createElement('p'); qp.className = 'adjust qp'; qp.textContent = 'Quick picks';
      picker.prepend(qp);
    }
    const fb = sheet && sheet.querySelector('.sheet-feedback');
    const acts = sheet && sheet.querySelector('.tm-sheet__actions');
    if (fb && acts) acts.prepend(fb);   // the result notice sits in the pinned actions, 16 above Add (A-12 / A-19)
  }
  if (screen === 'faster-signin-offer') {   // point 1 says the benefit once, by method (the subtitle already says "instead of an OTP")
    const t = document.querySelector('.points li:first-child .pt-t');
    const ic = (document.getElementById('hero-icon') || {}).dataset || {};
    const how = { fingerprint: 'one touch', 'face-id': 'a glance', face: 'a glance', lock: 'your PIN or pattern' }[ic.icon] || 'one touch';
    if (t) t.textContent = 'Sign in with ' + how;
  }
  if (screen === 'home-v3') {   // "Minimum 15 minutes" back on the Custom row (D-40)
    document.querySelectorAll('.frame .group .lbl').forEach(l => {
      if (l.textContent.trim() !== 'Custom' || l.querySelector('.help')) return;
      l.classList.add('with-help'); l.innerHTML = 'Custom<span class="help">Minimum 15 minutes</span>';
    });
  }
}
